From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pschatzmann <phil.schatzmann@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:07:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] v4l2: don't wait forever for buffers that never reached
 the firmware

start_streaming decremented count for every slot, including slots it
skipped, so a queued buffer in a later slot could stay unsent in
BUF_DRV_QUEUED. stop_streaming then calls vb2_wait_for_all_buffers(),
which waits for that buffer forever: the application hangs when it
closes the camera.

Walk all slots in start_streaming, and in stop_streaming return any
buffer still in BUF_DRV_QUEUED before waiting, as the firmware will
never return it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 fthd_v4l2.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fthd_v4l2.c b/fthd_v4l2.c
index 2120802..1904ba3 100644
--- a/fthd_v4l2.c
+++ b/fthd_v4l2.c
@@ -285,7 +285,7 @@ static int fthd_start_streaming(struct vb2_queue *vq, unsigned int count)
 	/* Starting the channel resets the ISP, so push the control values down. */
 	v4l2_ctrl_handler_setup(&dev_priv->v4l2_ctrl_handler);
 
-	for(i = 0; i < FTHD_BUFFERS && count; i++, count--) {
+	for(i = 0; i < FTHD_BUFFERS; i++) {
 		ctx = dev_priv->h2t_bufs + i;
 		if (ctx->state != BUF_DRV_QUEUED)
 			continue;
@@ -306,6 +306,16 @@ static void fthd_stop_streaming(struct vb2_queue *vq)
 	int ret, i;
 
 	ret = fthd_stop_channel(dev_priv, 0);
+
+	/* Buffers never sent to the firmware will not come back from it */
+	for(i = 0; i < FTHD_BUFFERS; i++) {
+		ctx = dev_priv->h2t_bufs + i;
+		if (ctx->state == BUF_DRV_QUEUED) {
+			ctx->state = BUF_ALLOC;
+			vb2_buffer_done(ctx->vb, VB2_BUF_STATE_ERROR);
+		}
+	}
+
 	if (!ret) {
 		pr_debug("waiting for buffers...\n");
 		vb2_wait_for_all_buffers(vq);
-- 
